Subject: [PATCH 52/54] fix(facts): the confirm card goes out with the reply
 that used the fact (1690)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tester's 49807: 0 of 2. Both seats' old employer fact WAS picked — the
fact_confirms row is there and confirm_asked_at was stamped at 00:35:18 and
00:36:56 — but no card reached the chat. The card carries no goal, and the
D617 filter (other goals come up only when the owner asks) held every
goal-less item on a run that did not look at goals. Nothing notes the card
again, and the fact was marked asked, so it was lost, not delayed.

A card about this very reply is not another goal's item: the fact-confirm
card now goes out with its reply, in a goal's conversation or outside one.
Everything else the filter holds stays held. The card's text and buttons are
1690's own, unchanged.

DONE WHEN: a search that leans on a core fact older than 180 days ends with
the one confirm line and its three taps, in a goal's conversation and
outside one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
